module

public import Physlib.QuantumMechanics.ComplexAction.WittAlgebraDerivation
public import Physlib.QuantumMechanics.ComplexAction.VirasoroCentralExtension

/-!
# Linking the genuine Witt Lie ring to the Virasoro structure constants

Three descriptions of the same algebra now live in the repository, and this module ties them together:

* `VirasoroCentralExtension` — the **abstract** Virasoro algebra by its structure constants and cocycle
  (`wittCoeff m n = m − n`, `virasoroCocycle c`, the descendant norm, the `sl(2)` null case).
* `WittAlgebraLieRing` — a **genuine `LieRing` object** for the finite global-conformal `sl(2,ℝ)`, in `2×2`
  matrices.
* `WittAlgebraDerivation` — the **genuine infinite-dimensional `LieRing` object**: the whole Witt algebra as
  derivations of `ℝ[T, T⁻¹]`, with `⁅L_m, L_n⁆ = (n − m) L_{m+n}` and Jacobi inherited from Mathlib.

## The realization identity

`wittGen_bracket_wittCoeff` proves that the concrete derivation bracket *is* the abstract structure
constant: `⁅L_m, L_n⁆ = wittCoeff(n, m) · L_{m+n}`. So the genuine Lie-algebra object of
`WittAlgebraDerivation` realizes exactly the structure constants that `VirasoroCentralExtension` characterizes
(the `wittCoeff(n,m) = n − m` here vs its `wittCoeff(m,n) = m − n` is the standard `L_m ↦ −L_m` sign of the
two conventions, an overall relabelling of the same algebra).

## The centreless case

Derivations of a commutative ring form a Lie algebra with **no** central extension — the Witt algebra is the
`c = 0` case of Virasoro. `virasoroCocycle_zero` records this: at central charge `c = 0` the Virasoro cocycle
vanishes identically, so `WittAlgebraDerivation` realizes precisely the centreless quotient. Reinstating
`c ≠ 0` is exactly the obstruction `virasoroCocycle c` (`VirasoroCentralExtension`), whose vacuum value is the
descendant norm `(c/12) n(n²−1)` and whose central charge `c` is the one whose ζ-regularized Casimir `−c/24`
is `Lorentz.SciamaFockVerlindeWitten.virasoroCasimir_from_zeta`, fixing the bosonic-string critical dimension
`D = 26` (`StringScaleHolographicGravity`). The infinitesimal conformal unitaries
`|Ψ⟩ = e^{iε(L_n + L_{−n})}|Ω⟩` of `ConformalModularEntanglement` are generated by these very `L_n`, and their
`n ∈ {−1, 0, 1}` global-conformal subalgebra is the Möbius `sl(2,ℝ)` realized in `WittAlgebraLieRing`.

## The `sl(2,ℝ)` global-conformal brackets

`wittGen_sl2` records the three defining brackets of the global-conformal subalgebra on the derivation
realization, matching `WittAlgebraLieRing.sl2_lie_ring_closes` up to the `L_m ↦ −L_m` convention.
-/

set_option autoImplicit false

@[expose] public section

namespace Physlib.QuantumMechanics.ComplexAction.WittVirasoroRealization

open Physlib.QuantumMechanics.ComplexAction.WittAlgebraDerivation
open Physlib.QuantumMechanics.ComplexAction.VirasoroCentralExtension

/-- **The derivation bracket realizes the abstract Witt structure constant.**  The genuine Lie bracket of
`WittAlgebraDerivation` is `wittCoeff` of `VirasoroCentralExtension`: `⁅L_m, L_n⁆ = wittCoeff(n,m) · L_{m+n}`
(`wittCoeff(n,m) = n − m`, the `L_m ↦ −L_m` convention of the structure-constant characterization). -/
theorem wittGen_bracket_wittCoeff (m n : ℤ) :
    ⁅wittGen m, wittGen n⁆ = ((wittCoeff n m : ℤ) : ℝ) • wittGen (m + n) := by
  rw [wittGen_bracket]
  congr 1
  rw [wittCoeff]; push_cast; ring

/-- **The derivation realization is centreless (`c = 0`).**  At central charge `c = 0` the Virasoro cocycle
vanishes identically — derivations of a commutative ring carry no central extension, so
`WittAlgebraDerivation` realizes the centreless (Witt) quotient of Virasoro. -/
theorem virasoroCocycle_zero (m n : ℤ) : virasoroCocycle 0 m n = 0 := by
  rw [virasoroCocycle]; split <;> simp

/-- **The global-conformal `sl(2,ℝ)` brackets on the derivation realization.**
`⁅L_1, L_{−1}⁆ = −2 L_0`, `⁅L_0, L_1⁆ = L_1`, `⁅L_0, L_{−1}⁆ = −L_{−1}` — the same `sl(2,ℝ)` as
`WittAlgebraLieRing.sl2_lie_ring_closes`, up to the `L_m ↦ −L_m` convention. -/
theorem wittGen_sl2 :
    ⁅wittGen 1, wittGen (-1)⁆ = (-2 : ℝ) • wittGen 0
      ∧ ⁅wittGen 0, wittGen 1⁆ = wittGen 1
      ∧ ⁅wittGen 0, wittGen (-1)⁆ = (-1 : ℝ) • wittGen (-1) := by
  refine ⟨?_, ?_, ?_⟩
  · have h := wittGen_bracket 1 (-1); norm_num at h; exact h
  · have h := wittGen_bracket 0 1; norm_num at h; exact h
  · have h := wittGen_bracket 0 (-1); norm_num at h; exact h

end Physlib.QuantumMechanics.ComplexAction.WittVirasoroRealization

end
